{"id": "c6aed666-a07c-444e-9761-38342ed6e7f1", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T03:50:32.843570", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "8673c360-3f74-4a3b-9d90-783b345705a5", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-203c0c3b-ea56-498d-9799-d0eb08952151", "tool_call": {"id": "call-203c0c3b-ea56-498d-9799-d0eb08952151", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Initial inspection: repo inventory, approach outline, assumptions\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## Initial inspection — three vehicles only\\n\\n### Vehicle 1 — Input / repository inspection\\n\\n**1.1 Local inventory (verified by file system traversal)**\\n\\n| Path | Status | Verified via |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `/workspace/task.json` | Present, 390 B | `ls -la /workspace`, sha256 = `83e037a30efe207a219988d927e3d31755f1b710202d2ae319cbeb35039459f3` |\\n| `/workspace/track.md` | **Referenced in `task.json` `documents` field but file NOT present** | `cat /workspace/track.md` → \\\"No such file or directory\\\" |\\n| `/home/actor/` | Empty directory | `ls -la` |\\n| `/root`, `/opt`, `/tmp` (research-content search) | No BBH / MinED / paper artefacts | `find / -maxdepth 4` filtered by `(bbh|mined|bigbench|hard|tasks|iclr|paper|source)` |\\n| Network | **disabled** (per `environment.network`) | Cannot resolve the gap by fetching externally |\\n| Preinstalled Python | 3.12.3 (`/bin/bash`; `which` missing) | `python3 -c \\\"import sys; print(sys.version)\\\"` |\\n\\nThe only on-disk artefact is `task.json`. Its `documents` field says: `track.md: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"` This declaration is itself confirmed locally, but the referenced `track.md` body is not available in the workspace. I cannot read it.\\n\\n**1.2 BBH benchmark metadata inventory**\\n\\n- (unconfirmed-locally) BBH = BIG-Bench Hard, Suzgun et al., 2022. Standard public eval design only (no train split), ~250 examples per task.\\n- (unconfirmed-locally) Composition: the canonical Suzgun BBH paper enumerates **23 tasks**. The user's framing of \\\"**27 tasks (23 MCQ + 4 free-form)**\\\" is a specific claim I cannot verify against the source from this workspace. I flag the 23 ↔ 27 discrepancy as unresolved and will defer the number to researcher confirmation.\\n- No BBH JSON, README, or `evaluate.py` is present locally.\\n- No reference to a canonical harness implementation can be cited from in-workspace material.\\n\\n**1.3 MinED / EM definitions inventory**\\n\\n- (unconfirmed-locally) MinED = Minimum Edit-Distance alignment criterion. The `researcher_topics` prefix `iclr2024/18013/4:setup_*` strongly suggests the source is ICLR 2024 paper id 18013. I cannot open this paper locally.\\n- (unconfirmed-locally) EM = Exact Match. Tentative prior: EM is the τ = 0 limit of MinED; this remains to be confirmed by the source paper.\\n- (unconfirmed-locally) Standard BBH EM canonicalization: lowercase + strip-ws + (for arithmetic tasks) numeric extraction. Not verifiable from in-workspace materials.\\n\\n**1.4 Empirical reproduction feasibility**\\n\\n- **No empirical reproduction is possible in this workspace.** No BBH data, no MinED reference implementation, no model checkpoints, no harness code, no GPU/CPU budget committed to compute.\\n- The remainder of this design therefore rests on **documented priors** (from my training-corpus knowledge), explicitly labelled as such. The researcher must independently verify every numeric or threshold claim before a result-stage handoff.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Vehicle 2 — Proposed approach (outline only; phase boundary respected)\\n\\n**(a) Research-question operationalization**\\n- MinED vs EM as RLHF-style alignment criterion, scored on BBH.\\n- Splits per task-type, reported separately then aggregated:\\n  - MCQ tasks (count to be confirmed — 23 per user; canonical Suzgun = 23) → reported as accuracy.\\n  - Free-form tasks (count to be confirmed — 4 per user) → reported as exact-match on canonicalized prediction.\\n- Working hypothesis to be tested, NOT pre-asserted here: aggregate MinED ≥ EM, with the largest deltas skewed toward free-form tasks where partial-credit information is recoverable by edit-distance scoring; near-zero delta on MCQ tasks where EM is already saturated.\\n\\n**(b) Independent / dependent variables**\\n- IV (two-level, within-subject): alignment criterion ∈ {EM, MinED}.\\n- DV: per-task BBH score.\\n- Aggregate DV: unweighted macro-mean over tasks (and secondary macro-mean within {MCQ, free-form}).\\n\\n**(c) Covariates / controls**\\n- Backbone: held fixed across arms OR matched within the same family (architecture, scale, pretraining). The design does not yet commit to \\\"fixed single backbone\\\" vs \\\"matched family\\\" — this is one of the items the researcher should confirm at result stage.\\n- Prompt template: identical strings across both arms. BBH canonical CoT prompt (Suzgun et al., or Kojima et al. zero-shot CoT — to be committed at result stage).\\n- Decoding: identical across criteria (greedy or fixed temperature/top-p with explicit seed protocol).\\n- RLHF pipeline: same preference pair dataset, same initial SFT policy, same KL coefficient, same optimization budget (steps / tokens). Only the alignment signal differs.\\n\\n**(d) Primary metric, per-task reporting, paired test outline**\\n- Per-task score vector (length = number of tasks, e.g. 27 if user's claim is correct).\\n- Primary aggregate: macro-mean over tasks.\\n- Planned inferential test: **paired Wilcoxon signed-rank** on per-task score deltas (non-parametric, robust to the small-N task count); equivalent fallback **paired t-test on score deltas** if approximate Gaussianity of the per-task delta vector can be plausibly argued. Report effect size (rank-biserial / Cohen's d_z) and a 95 % bootstrap CI over seeds if multi-seed.\\n- Honest small-N caveat: with ~25 task-deltas, statistical power is structurally limited; this is irreducible.\\n\\n**(e) MinED implementation outline slots — none yet committed**\\n- Edit-distance level: character-level vs BPE/token-level vs word-level (an open choice; affects scale and meaning).\\n- Normalization: ratio = distance / max(|gold|, |prediction|) → [0, 1]; alternative raw distance; needs source-paper confirmation.\\n- Threshold τ: scalar above which the response is treated as not-conforming; τ = 0 must recover EM as a sanity control.\\n- Gold-string comparison protocol: for MCQ, compare against the canonical choice letter; for free-form, compare against the gold answer after BBH canonicalization. Need source-paper alignment: does MinED compare against the chosen reference or against a set of valid forms?\\n- Stage of application: training-time reward, training-time gating, evaluation-time scoring, or a combination. Needs source-paper confirmation.\\n\\n**(f) Threats to validity — sources & candidate mitigations (only listed; not committed)**\\n\\n| Threat source | Mitigation slot |\\n|---|---|\\n| Backbone confound across arms | Hold backbone constant across arms |\\n| Prompt-side bias | Identical prompt + demonstrations |\\n| Decoding stochasticity | Greedy or ≥3 fixed seeds, average |\\n| Scale conflation MCQ vs free-form | Report per-type macro-mean in addition to global |\\n| Multiple comparisons across 25+ per-task tests | Pre-register 1 primary (global macro-mean); per-task = exploratory |\\n| Missing MinED source-paper config (τ, normalization, edit metric) | Researcher-verifies all numerical prescriptions before result stage |\\n| 23 vs 27 task-count ambiguity | Researcher confirms task list & composition; redesign aggregate if count differs |\\n| BBH held-out access constraints | Decided by user (download vs request API vs skip free-form subset) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Vehicle 3 — Consequential assumptions & uncertainties (each labelled)\\n\\n| # | Assumption | Label |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | BBH is held-out evaluation only (no train/val/test split) | `assumed-because-prior-knowledge-of-Suzgun-2022-BBH-design` (unconfirmed-locally) |\\n| 2 | BBH composition = 27 tasks (23 MCQ + 4 free-form) | `unconfirmed-locally` — canonical Suzgun is 23; user's 27 not verifiable in workspace |\\n| 3 | MinED source paper prescribes a specific threshold τ | `unconfirmed-locally` |\\n| 4 | MinED source paper prescribes a specific normalization (e.g. distance / max-length) | `unconfirmed-locally` |\\n| 5 | EM is recoverable as MinED at τ = 0 limit | `assumed-because-of-prior-knowledge` — needs paper confirmation |\\n| 6 | BBH EM evaluation canonicalization = lowercase + strip-ws + arithmetic-eval | `assumed-because-of-BBH-canonical-protocol` — unconfirmed-locally |\\n| 7 | Backbone choice: a specific GPT variant (e.g. `text-davinci-002`) or open-source (LLaMA / Mistral) is canonical for this comparison | `unconfirmed` — would best come from the MinED paper's reported experiment |\\n| 8 | Multi-run seed strategy = ≥ 3 seeds (default; 5 if budget permits) | `assumed-default-3-to-5` — to be confirmed at result stage |\\n| 9 | Demonstration pool = BBH chain-of-thought prompt (Suzgun et al., few-shot hand-crafted) OR Kojima et al. zero-shot CoT (\\\"Let's think step by step\\\") | `assumed-because-BBH-canonical` — choice changes accuracy non-trivially |\\n| 10 | Source-paper numerical claims (MinED > EM on BBH) will NOT be empirically re-derived (only hypothetically contrasted in narrative) | `confirmed-by-environment-constraints` — runtime + repo absent |\\n| 11 | Paired Wilcoxon signed-rank is the planned primary inferential test | `assumed-because-small-N` — will be locked at result stage |\\n| 12 | MinED applies during RLHF training (as opposed to evaluation-time scoring only) | `unconfirmed` — paper-level decision |\\n| 13 | `track.md` referenced in `task.json` cannot be inspected here; the only in-file hint is its quoted one-line description | `confirmed-by-failed-read-attempt` |\\n| 14 | Network disabled precludes external lookup of BBH metadata, MinED paper, or evaluation harness | `confirmed-by-environment.network-field` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Phase-boundary declaration**: This is a plan-stage handoff. No full design committed; no metrics frozen; no implementation sketched beyond outline slots; no external system queried; no compute invoked. Awaiting researcher approval (`approve_approach=true`) before producing the result-stage design.\",\"evidence\":\"**Local /workspace evidence (executed checks):**\\n\\n- `ls -la /workspace` → only `task.json` (390 B) present; nothing else.\\n- `sha256sum /workspace/task.json` → `83e037a30efe207a219988d927e3d31755f1b710202d2ae319cbeb35039459f3` (file integrity confirmed).\\n- `cat /workspace/track.md` → \\\"No such file or directory\\\" — file referenced in `task.json.documents` does not exist on disk.\\n- `find /workspace -maxdepth 3` → only `task.json`. No subdirectories. No BBH data, MinED source, README, eval harness, model checkpoints, or supplementary PDFs.\\n- `ls -la /home/actor/` → directory exists, empty.\\n- Broad search `find / -maxdepth 5 -iname \\\"*iclr*|*paper*|*source*\\\"` filtered by `(bbh|mined|bigbench|hard|tasks)` → no matches (only LibreOffice `.properties` files were matched and explicitly discarded).\\n- `env | grep -iE \\\"(paper|track|research|src|doc)\\\"` → no environment variables hint at pre-loaded source paths.\\n- `task.json` content verified verbatim; its `documents` field declares only `track.md` with body `Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.`\\n\\n**Provenance-gapped items (not in this workspace):**\\n\\n- BBH canonical composition (23 vs 27 tasks, MCQ vs free-form split) — not verifiable from any local artefact.\\n- MinED paper (suggested id `iclr2024/18013`) — not present; its τ / normalization / edit-metric prescriptions cannot be cited from local evidence.\\n- Evaluation harness reference (BBH `evaluate.py`) — not present; env has `python3 3.12.3` but no project dependencies and no code repo.\\n- EM canonicalization specifics for BBH — not locally documented.\\n- Network is disabled per `environment.network` — no external lookup permitted.\\n\\nNo executed experiment; no numeric contrast invented; hostile-trust flagged items 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 12 in Vehicle 3 are explicitly marked unconfirmed-locally and require researcher verification before the result-stage handoff.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Backbone: agnostic in plan; will be committed only after user supplies an allowed family (per environment constraints, no compute is available).</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Multi-seed default = ≥ 3 seeds (assumed-default; to be tightened at result stage).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"EM canonicalization in BBH uses lowercase + strip-ws + arithmetic extraction (prior knowledge; unconfirmed-locally).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"MinED is a minimum edit-distance alignment criterion with a tunable threshold τ; τ = 0 recovers EM (per prior knowledge; not locally verifiable).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BBH canonical task count is 23 (Suzgun original); the user's framing of \\\"27 tasks (23 MCQ + 4 free-form)\\\" cannot be confirmed locally and may reflect a derivative taxonomy.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"BBH = BIG-Bench Hard, Suzgun et al. 2022; held-out evaluation only (per prior knowledge; not locally verifiable).</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Whether demonstration pool is BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun) or zero-shot CoT (Kojima) — affects absolute scores and possibly rank.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"The exact 27-task BBH composition implied by the user — task mapping to MCQ/free-form and subset inclusion/exclusion is unverified.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Whether the researcher wants the design to (i) pre-suppose MinED > EM and seek the magnitude, or (ii) stay null-hypothesis-neutral — affects language and pre-registration.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether comparison is against (i) a single ca