{"id": "56de2324-4950-48de-ba64-d910567733be", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T03:55:34.398785", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7ef414f6-54dc-420c-b7ca-e3c6f236edd5", "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# Result-Stage Design Document\n**Question.** For Alignment Criteria, does the proposed MinED method outperform EM method, on benchmark BBH?\n**Track contract.** Design-only. Empirical reproduction is OUT of scope. All numeric content is symbolic or labelled as source-paper-pending. No fabricated BBH score, no invented τ value treated as ground truth.\n\n---\n\n## Section 1 — Research question re-stated with operationalization\n\n**Re-statement.** After locking 5 constraints from the reviewer's brief:\n\n- **Alignment criterion** is treated as the *RLHF objective / reward-shaping function* used during training (and secondarily the evaluation-time scorer) for a single fixed backbone.\n- **MinED** = a minimum edit-distance alignment criterion operating on (generation, gold/chosen-response) pairs, with a tunable threshold τ and a normalization to a [0, 1] scale, augmented by an ε-completion bonus. (Definition pending source-paper confirmation; see Section 4.)\n- **EM** = an exact-match criterion operating on (canonicalized generation, canonicalized gold), with rewards in {0, 1}. (BBH canonicalization assumed; see Section 3.)\n- **\"Outperform on BBH\"** is operationalized as: greater aggregate BBH score under the MinED arm than under the EM arm, measured as the paired per-task mean-difference over the 27 locked tasks.\n\n**Operationalizing the comparison.**\n- The two arms share exactly one backbone, one prompt string, one decoding policy, one preference dataset, one SFT checkpoint, one KL coefficient, and one optimization budget. Only the alignment criterion varies.\n- The outcome is a 27-dimensional paired vector Δ_i = score^{MinED}_i − score^{EM}_i (with optional seed-mean if multi-seed).\n- The primary scalar is the global macro-mean over Δ, the global wine being the **primary pre-registered metric**.\n- A structurally deducible **directional sanity constraint**: since EM is recoverable as MinED in the τ → 0 limiting case (Section 4 slot v), MinED is never structurally worse than EM on a per-example basis; any aggregate gain must come from cases where EM is brittle — primarily free-form tasks — not from cases where EM is already saturated — primarily MCQ tasks. This is a **structural** observation, not an empirical one, and bounds the question rather than answering it.\n\n---\n\n## Section 2 — Experimental arms + IV/DV/covariates table\n\n| Element | Specification | Confirmation status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Arm A — EM | Reward = 𝟙[canonical(pred) == canonical(gold)] (canonicalize per Section 3) | design default; source-paper confirmation pending |\n| Arm B — MinED | Reward = (1 − normalized_edit_distance) + ε · completion_bonus, gated by τ; 0 (floor) when normalized_distance > τ | design default; source-paper confirmation pending (Section 4) |\n| **Independent variable (IV)** | Alignment criterion ∈ {EM, MinED}; two-level, within-subject over tasks | locked |\n| **Dependent variable (DV), per task** | BBH accuracy on task i ∈ {1,…,27} | locked |\n| **Primary aggregate DV** | Global macro-mean over the 27 per-task accuracies | locked (pre-registered) |\n| **Secondary aggregate DVs** | MCQ-only macro-mean (n=23); free-form-only macro-mean (n=4) | locked |\n| Backbone (controlled, **NOT varied**) | One single fixed backbone across both arms. Designated \"MinED-paper-canonical, identity TBD\". Plausible class per documented prior: text-davinci-002 family or open-source equivalent at comparable scale. | identity pending source-paper confirmation |\n| Demonstration protocol (PRIMARY) | BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun et al. canonical exemplars) | locked |\n| Demonstration protocol (SECONDARY, appendix) | Zero-shot CoT (Kojima et al., \"Let's think step by step\") | locked |\n| Decoding | Greedy | locked |\n| Seeds | n_seeds = 1 (single-run reporting), 3 (multi-seed reporting, mean across seeds per arm per task) | locked |\n| Prompt string | Identical byte-for-byte across both arms | locked |\n| Pair dataset | Identical across both arms | locked |\n| SFT starting checkpoint | Identical across both arms | locked |\n| KL coefficient | Identical across both arms | locked |\n| Optimization budget (steps, tokens) | Identical across both arms | locked |\n| RLHF algorithm family (e.g., PPO, DPO, IPO) | Identical across both arms | locked |\n\n**Justification of foundational concept (good-faith friendliness).** A \"macro-mean\" is the unweighted mean of per-task scores; alternative is a \"micro-mean\" which weights each example equally and can be dominated by large tasks. Macro-mean is the BBH-canonical aggregate because BBH tasks have approximately equal example counts (~250 each per Suzgun-2022 documented prior), and macro-mean treats every task as an equally-weighted voice in the headline.\n\n---\n\n## Section 3 — BBH evaluation protocol with locked task list and MCQ/free-form split\n\n**Locked composition** (per study_context `iclr2024/18013/4:setup_14`):\n- Total = 27 tasks.\n- Subset MCQ = 23 tasks → scored by accuracy on canonical choice letter.\n- Subset free-form = 4 tasks → scored by canonicalized exact-match against gold string.\n\n**Historical-context footnote (canonical Suzgun accounting).** Suzgun et al. 2022 (\"Challenging BIG-Bench Tasks and Whether Chain-of-Thought Can Solve Them\") names **23 task families** in prose, including reasoning (causal judgement, formal fallacies, snarks, sports understanding), algorithmic (boolean expressions, dyck languages, multistep arithmetic, navigate, word sorting, object counting), and lookup/reasoning (date understanding, hyperbaton, movie recommendation, penguins in a table, ruin names, salient translation, geometric shapes, temporal sequences, web of lies, disambiguation QA, reasoning about colored objects). The 27-task accounting used here corresponds to the BBH-YAML task-config taxonomy on the canonical BBH GitHub release, in which `logical_deduction_three_objects / five / seven` and `tracking_shuffled_objects_three_objects / five / seven` are counted as six distinct configs rather than two families. **Suzgun reference is documented prior only; not locally verifiable in this workspace.** The locked 27-task design-of-record treats canonical task names as confirmation-pending to the source-paper / experiment-script `tasks/` directory.\n\n**Per-task fields to populate at confirmation time** (design-stage schema, no committed values except for `default_prompt_template`):\n\n| Field | Default | Confirmation |\n|---|---|---|\n| task_id | string matching Suzgun YAML convention (e.g., `bbh:boolean_expressions`) | pending |\n| task_name | display string | pending |\n| task_type ∈ {MCQ, free-form} | as locked split | locked |\n| n_examples | ≈ 250 per Suzgun convention; cite exact when confirmed | pending |\n| default_prompt_template | BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun canonical) | locked |\n| scoring function (MCQ) | canonical choice letter; tie-break = regex `\\(\\w\\)` then first uppercase token | locked as design-stage; pending comparison with Suzgun parser |\n| scoring function (free-form) | lowercase + strip-whitespace + collapse internal ws + arithmetic numeric extraction | locked as design-stage; pending source-paper confirmation (study_context confirmation pending) |\n\n**Free-form scoring canonicalization (design-stage default, source-paper confirmation pending):**\n1. Lowercase the prediction string.\n2. Strip leading/trailing whitespace.\n3. Collapse runs of internal whitespace to single space.\n4. If task is arithmetic (e.g., `multistep_arithmetic_two`), extract numeric value via regex `±?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?`; compare as floats.\n5. Exact-string match against canonicalized gold.\n\n**MCQ scoring canonicalization** maps generation to (A), (B), (C), (D) … depending on choice letter; tie-break order: regex `\\(\\w\\)` then first uppercase single-letter token. (Documented-prior BBH protocol; not locally verified.)\n\n**Held-out status (no BBH training):** BBH examples are used only for evaluation in both arms; no BBH example is consumed by SFT, RM training, or RL training. **Status**: assumed-because-prior-knowledge-of-Suzgun-BBH-design; unconfirmed-locally.\n\n**Decoding and seeding:** greedy, n_seeds ∈ {1, 3}. With n_seeds = 3, the reported per-task accuracy per arm is the mean across 3 seeds.\n\n---\n\n## Section 4 — MinED operationalization (default config + source-paper confirmation flags)\n\nThe 6 implementation slots from the reviewer's Lock 5 are tabulated with (a) locked design-stage default, (b) rationale, (c) source-paper confirmation flag.\n\n| Slot | Locked design-stage default | Rationale | Source-paper confirmation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| (i) Edit-distance level | **Character-level PRIMARY** (Levenshtein over Unicode codepoints); **BPE/token-level ACCEPTABLE SECONDARY** | Char-level is tokenizer-agnostic and reproducible. BPE-level requires tokenizer alignment with backbone and so couples the metric to the backbone family. | pending |\n| (ii) Normalization | **ratio = Levenshtein(pred, gold) / max(\\|gold\\|, \\|prediction\\|)** ∈ [0, 1] PRIMARY; raw Levenshtein distance as SECONDARY reporting | Bounding the metric to [0, 1] yields scale-invariant rewards interpretable as \"fraction of the longer string that must change to match the shorter\". Raw distance preserved for diagnostics. | pending |\n| (iii) Reward formulation | `reward(pred, gold) = 1 − normalized_distance + ε · completion_bonus`, where ε > 0 (design-stage default = 1e-3) and `completion_bonus = 1` if the generation's structural envelope matches gold (matched by length bucket: same number of structured elements as gold, e.g., equal number of closing brackets, equal number of arithmetic operands, equal number of sorted words), else 0. If `normalized_distance > τ`, the reward collapses to a floor value (default = 0). | 1 − normalized_distance ∈ [0, 1] is the principal signal; ε-completion bonus prevents the policy from hacking by truncation to a sub-segment of gold; the τ-gate prevents rewarding structurally-wrong generations. | pending — formulation matches reviewer's brief; exact ε, completion-bonus definition, and floor value to be cross-checked against source-paper |\n| (iv) Threshold τ | Scalar training-time gate. Design-stage τ-grid = {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0}. Each τ is a separate sub-arm of Arm B; the headline τ is the one maximizing primary pre-registered metric; sensitivity reported across all τ. | τ = 0 must collapse MinED to EM (slot v); τ = 1.0 sets the gate to \"always pass\". | pending — paper may use a different τ or τ-grid; cross-check required |\n| (v) **SANITY CONTROL** = τ → 0 ⇒ EM | **Pre-computation gate**: implement, run MinED with τ = 0 on a synthetic batch (e.g., 100 hand-crafted pred/gold pairs spanning exact matches, off-by-whitespace, off-by-letter, off-by-word, fully-disjoint strings); assert reward equals EM within tolerance `ε_sanity = 1e-6` pointwise; if any assertion fails, BLOCK downstream runs and report failure. | Slot v is the only slot whose correctness can be checked without source-paper credentials — because τ = 0 reduces MinED to a definitional limit. Failing this gate means implementation is bugged. | confirmed-as-design-discipline |\n| (vi) Stage of application | **Training-time reward PRIMARY**: MinED scores each minibatch's generations during RL training, providing the gradient-bearing signal. **Evaluation-time scoring SECONDARY**: under either arm's policy, evaluate using MinED-as-scorer as a diagnostic (i.e., what would MinED have said about EM-arm generations and vice versa). | Training-time is where the criterion effects policy gradients; evaluation-time secondary reporting reveals whether gains survive a metric-swap. | pending — source-paper's split between training-time reward vs evaluation-time scorer must be confirmed |\n\n**Note on slot interactions.** Slots (ii) and (iii) jointly determine the reward mapping. Slot (iv) determines the active gate. The sanity control (slot v) is the only universally checkable invariant. Slots (i), (iii), (iv), (vi) together comprise what the source paper would have to document for us to use its numbers — currently all four are confirmation-pending.\n\n**Cross-cutting default for the τ-floor.** When `normalized_distance > τ`, reward = 0 (the design-stage floor). Whether the source paper uses 0, a small negative, or a shaping function here is confirmation-pending.\n\n---\n\n## Section 5 — Statistical analysis plan with pre-registration\n\n### 5.1 Pre-registered primary\n\n- **Unit of analysis** = task (n = 27). Each task yields one paired delta Δ_i = score^{MinED}_i − score^{EM}_i, aggregated across seeds as the mean (n_seeds = 3) or the single value (n_seeds = 1).\n- **Pre-registered scalar** = global macro-mean Δ̄ = (1/27) Σ_i Δ_i.\n- **Pre-registered test** = paired **Wilcoxon signed-rank**, two-sided, α = 0.05, on the 27 Δ̄_i values.\n- **Effect size** = **rank-biserial correlation r_rb** with bootstrap 95% CI computed over seeds (B = 1 000 resamples when n_seeds ≥ 3; degenerate when n_seeds = 1 — reported as NA).\n- **Reportable summary** = {median Δ, signed-rank W, two-sided p, r_rb, 95% CI}.\n\n**Justification of foundational concept (good-faith friendliness).** Wilcoxon signed-rank is a non-parametric test that ranks the absolute values of pairwise differences, then sums the ranks of positive-signed differences and tests whether that sum departs significantly from its null expectation under symmetric zero-median. It is the standard paired alternative to the paired t-test when the number of pairs is small (~25), when the differences cannot be assumed Gaussian, or when the experimenter wishes to be robust to a single outlying task distorting the mean. The paired t-test, by contrast, computes (mean Δ) / (sd Δ / √n) under normality assumptions. Rank-biserial correlation r_rb = (W⁺ − W⁻)/(W⁺ + W⁻), bounded in [−1, +1]; a positive r_rb says more positive-signed differences, i.e., MinED > EM direction.\n\n### 5.2 Pre-registered secondaries\n\n- **MCQ-only macro-mean** Δ^{MCQ} over n = 23 task-deltas; same test family.\n- **Free-form-only macro-mean** Δ^{FF} over n = 4 task-deltas; same test family **but UNDERPOWERED**: with n = 4 pairs, no inferential test has adequate power to reject the null under realistic effect sizes; report descriptively (point estimate, sign, range) only. Flagged explicitly as such.\n- **Global macro-mean over per-seed triples** is identical to primary by construction; not a separate test.\n\n### 5.3 Exploratory status (not pre-registered; multiple-comparison caveat applies)\n\n- Per-task headline accuracy per arm (27 entries × 2 arms) — descriptive only.\n- Per-task inference (sign test or per-task bootstrap CI) — no family-wise correction is applied; per-task results carry an inflated false-positive warning.\n- Stratification by sub-family (algorithmic / linguistic / logical / symbolic) — descriptive.\n- Stratification by demonstration pool (few-shot vs zero-shot) — appendix only.\n- Seed-sensitivity scatter (Δ̄_i vs seed index) — appendix only.\n\n### 5.4 Pre-registration code-level commitments\n\n- **Pairing rule** = per-task Δ_i defined once a score exists for both arms in seed s on task i; otherwise that task in seed s is dropped. Missing-task exclusion is symmetric across arms.\n- **Cross-seed aggregation** = for n_seeds = 3, per-task Δ̄_i is the mean across the 3 surviving per-seed Δ_i; a task is dropped entirely from all seeds if dropped in any seed (to preserve pairing for the final cross-seed Wilcoxon).\n- **Determinism** = greedy decoding reduces per-seed variance to 0 for a given prompt; n_seeds > 1 in this design captures *seeds over RL training stochasticity* (e.g., minibatch shuffle seed), not decoding stochasticity.\n\n### 5.5 Honest small-N caveat (carried to result-stage report)\n\n- With N = 27 pairs, paired Wilcoxon at α = 0.05 two-sided achieves 80% power only at standardized effect δ/σ ≈ 0.55 (i.e., Cohen's d_z ≥ ~0.55). Smaller true effects — even if present — will yield non-significant p-values.\n- N = 4 pairs (free-form subset) → effectively zero inferential power; pre-registered as descriptive-only.\n- Consequence: a non-significant Wilcoxon in this design does NOT establish \"no difference\", only \"no detectable difference at medium-to-large effect size\".\n\n---\n\n## Section 6 — Threats to validity and mitigations\n\n| # | Threat | Source of threat | Mitigation locked in this design |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Backbone confound | Different backbones across arms would invalidate paired comparison | Single fixed backbone across both arms (Lock 2) |\n| 2 | Prompt-side bias | Different prompt strings across arms | Identical byte-for-byte prompt to both arms |\n| 3 | Demonstration exemplar bias | Different few-shot exemplars across arms | Same exemplar copy-pasted across both arms; PRIMARY = Suzgun canonical; SECONDARY = Kojima zero-shot (appendix) |\n| 4 | Decoding stochasticity | Greedy deterministic at decoding; cross-run variance only at training-time stochasticity | Greedy default; n_seeds ≥ 3 for cross-training-seed reporting |\n| 5 | MCQ vs free-form scale conflation | Free-form tasks have lower absolute scores; macro-mean mixing them is a heterogeneous average | Report per-type (MCQ vs free-form) macro-mean alongside global (Section 5) |\n| 6 | Multiple comparisons across 27 per-task tests | Inflated family-wise false-positive rate | Pre-register 1 primary (global); MCQ/FF secondaries; per-task = exploratory (Section 5.3) |\n| 7 | Task count ambiguity (23 vs 27) | Suzgun 23-task prose vs YAML/config 27-task accounting | Anchored to 27 per study_context; Suzgun 23-task referred to in footnote only |\n| 8 | Free-form subset underpower | n = 4 pairs | Descriptive-only on free-form sub-aggregate; primary on global 27-task |\n| 9 | Source-paper τ-grid unverified | Source paper may report a specific τ or τ-grid | Sensitivity report across design-stage {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0} τ-grid (Section 4 slot iv) |\n| 10 | Source-paper edit-distance level unverified | Char vs BPE affects reward scale and interpretation | Char primary; BPE reported as secondary (Section 4 slot i) |\n| 11 | Source-paper reward formulation unverified | ε-completion bonus + floor penalty specifics | Design defaults committed; explicitly pending (Section 4 slot iii) |\n| 12 | Source-paper stage of application unverified | Training-time vs evaluation-time use determines what is being compared | Design committed to training-time primary, evaluation-time secondary; both reported (Section 4 slot vi) |\n| 13 | Sanity-control (τ=0 ⇒ EM) failure | Implementation bug under any of slots (i)-(iv) | Pre-execution gate blocks the run on failure (Section 4 slot v) |\n| 14 | BBH held-out not strictly held-out | MinED paper might have trained on BBH contamination | Audit of MinED paper's training data declaration; flagged for researcher |\n| 15 | track.md content unverified | File referenced in task.json but absent from /workspace | Quoted one-line body is the only track.md content available; treated as binding contract (\"design-only, no repo, no compute, no empirics\") |\n| 16 | Network disabled | Cannot resurrect MinED paper / BBH script locally | Section 4's confirmation-pending column carries this liability |\n| 17 | RLHF algorithm family not pinned | PPO vs DPO vs IPO etc. may shift baseline expectation | Identical algorithm family across arms; family identity marked \"locked, exact identity TBD consistent with MinED paper\" |\n\n---\n\n## Section 7 — Feasibility and scope-limits (derived from environment)\n\n### 7.1 Environment-confirmed facts (re-derived from /workspace)\n\n| Fact | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| /workspace contains only `task.json` (390 B) | `ls -la /workspace`; sha256 = `83e037a30efe207a219988d927e3d31755f1b710202d2ae319cbeb35039459f3` |\n| `track.md` is referenced in `task.json.documents` but is NOT on disk | `cat /workspace/track.md` → \"No such file or directory\" |\n| Only body of `track.md` available = its quoted one-line description | `task.json`: `documents.track.md = \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"` |\n| /home/actor/ exists but is empty | `ls -la /home/actor/` |\n| No BBH JSON, no MinED paper, no harness code, no model checkpoints, no `evaluate.py`, no `tasks/` directory | `find / -maxdepth 5` filtered by bbh/mined/bigbench/hard/tasks/iclr/paper/source → no relevant matches |\n| Network disabled | `environment.network = \"disabled\"` (per task input) |\n| Python 3.12.3 available; no project dependencies preinstalled | `python3 -c \"import sys; print(sys.version)\"` |\n| GPU not enabled | `environment.gpu_enabled = false` |\n| CPU affinity = 24; runtime = bubblewrap; datasets = [] (explicitly empty) | task input |\n\n### 7.2 Scope-limit implications\n\n1. **Empirical reproduction is OUT of scope.** No τ-grid is run, no per-task score table is produced, no paired Wilcoxon statistic is computed in this workspace. This document is a protocol, not a result.\n2. **Source-paper confirmation is the researcher's responsibility.** The 27-task list, the τ-grid, the edit-distance level, the normalization rule, the ε-completion bonus, and the training-time vs evaluation-time split are all **confirmation-pending** items in Section 4. Defaults in this design are *plausible priors*, not *established fact*.\n3. **\"Outperform\" claim, downstream.** Any future narrative that says \"MinED outperforms EM on BBH\" must remain a hypothetical-contrast around the design, not an assertion of a numerical gap. The directional sanity constraint in Section 1 establishes that EM ⊆ MinED-as-τ→0, so any future empirical context must respect that MinED is structurally never worse per-example — meaning any *aggregate* gap, if reported, would be an aggregate phenomenon emerging from free-form partial-credit rather than a uniform per-example effect.\n4. **Numeric inventory across this document** — every number is one of:\n   - **Symbolic / structural**: 27 tasks, 23 MCQ + 4 free-form, α = 0.05, n_seeds = 3, B = 1 000 bootstrap resamples, τ-grid {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0}, ε = 1e-3, ε_sanity = 1e-6, signed-rank W, rank-biserial r_rb.\n   - **Plausible-prior / locked-default**: backbone identity \"TBD\", ~250 examples per task (Suzgun convention), greedy decoding.\n   - **Source-paper-pending**: exact 27-task task_ids, exact τ or τ-grid in the MinED paper, exact ε value, exact completion-bonus definition, exact backbone identity, exact algorithm family (PPO/DPO/IPO/etc.).\n5. **No fabricated BBH per-task accuracy, no invented \"MinED = X%, EM = Y% on aggregate\", no invented Cohen's d_z** appears in this document. The result of an experiment is not within scope, was not attempted, and is not claimed.\n\n### 7.3 Out-of-scope but acknowledged\n\n- The actual RLHF training run.\n- The actual BBH inference pass.\n- The actual reward-model training.\n- Any cost / wall-clock estimate (no access to compute).\n- Any claim about real numerical comparison of MinED vs EM on BBH.\n\n### 7.4 In-scope deliverable\n\nThis document — Sections 1 through 7 above — is the deliverable of the design phase. Hand-off to a *separate* execution phase (out of scope here) would require resolving every \"confirmation-pending\" item in Section 4 plus the backbone identity in Section 2, all of which are document-spec externalities, not inferable from /workspace.\n\n---\n\n**End of result-stage design document.** No experiment executed. No numbers fabricated. All design assumptions carry source-paper-pending flags where the source paper is not available locally. Awaiting reviewer nod to lock or revise.", "evidence": "**Strong provenance (locally verified):**\n- /workspace inventory: only `task.json` (390 B), sha256 verified.\n- track.md absent on disk; only its quoted one-line body is available via `task.json.documents`.\n- Network disabled; python3 3.12.3 available; no project dependencies.\n- /home/actor/ empty; no BBH/MinED artefacts anywhere in the filesystem (broad find with name filters bbh/mined/bigbench/hard/tasks/iclr/paper/source returned only LibreOffice .properties files, explicitly discarded).\n\n**Documented prior (NOT locally verified — cited where used):**\n- Suzgun et al. 2022 \"Challenging BIG-Bench Tasks and Whether Chain-of-Thought Can Solve Them\" — BBH introduced; 23 task families listed in prose; ~250 examples per task; held-out evaluation only. Cited as historical-context footnote in Section 3 and as candidate for backbone identification in Section 2.\n- BBH GitHub YAML-config taxonomy — 27 distinct task configs (Logical Deduction × 3, Tracking Shuffled × 3 counted separately). Cited as the basis for the 27-task design-of-record per study_context.\n- Kojima et al. zero-shot CoT (\"Let's think step by step\") prompt template. Cited as appendix-level alternative.\n- Wilcoxon signed-rank, rank-biserial correlation, macro-mean — textbook statistical concepts, briefly justified in Section 5.\n\n**Confirmation-pending (NOT verified, NOT in /workspace):**\n- MinED paper at `iclr2024/18013` — τ-grid, normalization rule, edit-distance level, ε value, completion-bonus definition, training/evaluation split, backbone identity, RLHF algorithm family. All flagged in Section 4 and Section 6.\n- 27-task exact task_ids and per-task MCQ/free-form classification — anchored to study_context framing; not reconciled against source.\n- BBH EM scoring canonicalization specifics for arithmetic numeric extraction — design-stage default committed; confirmation-pending.\n\n**No fabricated numerics:** No BBH per-task accuracy values, no τ-specific MinED/EM gap numbers, no invented Cohen's d_z, no claim that a run was performed. All numerics in the document are either symbolic (paired design constants), plausible-prior, or confirmation-pending labels.\n\n**Locked per reviewer brief (applied verbatim):**\n- Lock 1 — 27 tasks (23 MCQ + 4 free-form) anchored; Suzgun 23 relegated to footnote.\n- Lock 2 — Single fixed backbone (identity TBD pending source-paper).\n- Lock 3 — BBH few-shot CoT primary; Kojima zero-shot secondary (appendix); greedy decoding; identical prompt-string; n_seeds ∈ {1, 3}.\n- Lock 4 — Global macro-mean pre-registered as primary; MCQ-only / free-form-only as secondaries; paired Wilcoxon two-sided α=0.05; rank-biserial with 95% bootstrap CI; small-N caveat explicit.\n- Lock 5 — MinED slots (i)-(vi) committed with defaults; source-paper confirmation flag column on every slot; sanity control (τ=0 ⇒ EM) with pre-execution gate.", "assumptions": ["Single fixed backbone across both arms, identity designation \"MinED-paper-canonical, TBD\". Backbone is not a variability dimension.", "Demonstration protocol PRIMARY = BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun canonical); SECONDARY = zero-shot CoT (Kojima), appendix only.", "Greedy decoding is the decoding rule; cross-seed variance captures training-time, not decoding, stochasticity.", "BBH 27-task design-of-record per study_context iclr2024/18013/4:setup_14; Suzgun 23-task prose is footnote only.", "MinED slot (i) edit-distance level = char-level primary, BPE-level secondary. Aggregated as the principal reward in slot (iii).", "MinED slot (ii) ratio normalization = Levenshtein / max(|gold|,|prediction|) in [0,1]; raw Levenshtein reported as secondary diagnostic only.", "MinED slot (iii) reward = 1 − normalized_distance + ε·completion_bonus with floor = 0 when normalized_distance > τ; ε default = 1e-3, completion_bonus definition design-stage.", "MinED slot (iv) τ-grid = {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0}; τ=0 mandatory as sanity control.", "MinED slot (v) sanity control = pre-execution gate that MinED-at-τ=0 equals EM within ε_sanity = 1e-6 on a 100-pair synthetic batch; run is blocked on failure.", "MinED slot (vi) stage of application = training-time reward primary, evaluation-time scorer secondary reporting.", "BBH free-form scoring canonicalization = lowercase + strip-ws + collapse internal ws + arithmetic numeric extraction (regex ±?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+?) for arithmetic tasks).", "Paired Wilcoxon signed-rank two-sided α=0.05; rank-biserial r_rb; bootstrap 95% CI with B=1000; n_seeds=1 reports no CI, n_seeds=3 reports CI.", "Per-task headline scores exploratory only; multiple-comparison caveat uncorrected (no Bonferroni).", "Free-form subset (n=4) is reported descriptively only due to structural underpower."], "uncertainties": ["MinED paper's exact τ or τ-grid, edit-distance level, normalization rule, ε value, completion-bonus definition, training/evaluation split, backbone identity, RLHF algorithm family — all source-paper-pending. Defaults in Section 4 are documented priors, not ground truth.", "Exact 27-task task_ids and per-task MCQ/free-form classification — anchored to study_context framing but not locally verifiable.", "Whether BBH evaluation harness applies lowercase + strip-ws canonicalization uniformly across MCQ and free-form tasks and whether arithmetic tasks require numeric extraction — design-stage default; not locally verified.", "Whether MinED paper trains on BBH explicitly (potential held-out contamination) — to be checked at source-paper confirmation.", "Whether demonstrate-on-BBH-few-shot vs Kojima-zero-shot changes magnitude or sign of Δ — handled via appendix stratification but not pre-registered.", "Whether the seed-multi-run statistic reflects training stochasticity (intended) or some other source — depends on RLHF loop implementation, which is confirmation-pending.", "Whether the underlying RLHF signal (PPO vs DPO vs IPO etc.) materially affects the magnitude of MinED-vs-EM gap — held constant across arms but family-agnostic in this design.", "Whether direction \"MinED ≥ EM\" holds in aggregate — design carries a structural sanity bound (EM ⊆ MinED-as-τ→0) which means per-example MinED is never worse than EM, but aggregate behavior depends on the partial-credit density of free-form tasks and is not pre-asserted."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-2d986814-0ee1-44ce-8432-a1ec51788f06", "tool_call": {"id": "call-2d986814-0ee1-44ce-8432-a1ec51788f06", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Result-stage design document \\u2014 7 sections, design-only, locks 1\\u20135 honored\", \"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# Result-Stage Design Document\\n**Question.** For Alignment Criteria, does the proposed MinED method outperform EM method, on benchmark BBH?\\n**Track contract.** Design-only. Empirical reproduction is OUT of scope. All numeric content is symbolic or labelled as source-paper-pending. No fabricated BBH score, no invented \\u03c4 value treated as ground truth.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 1 \\u2014 Research question re-stated with operationalization\\n\\n**Re-statement.** After locking 5 constraints from the reviewer's brief:\\n\\n- **Alignment criterion** is treated as the *RLHF objective / reward-shaping function* used during training (and secondarily the evaluation-time scorer) for a single fixed backbone.\\n- **MinED** = a minimum edit-distance alignment criterion operating on (generation, gold/chosen-response) pairs, with a tunable threshold \\u03c4 and a normalization to a [0, 1] scale, augmented by an \\u03b5-completion bonus. (Definition pending source-paper confirmation; see Section 4.)\\n- **EM** = an exact-match criterion operating on (canonicalized generation, canonicalized gold), with rewards in {0, 1}. (BBH canonicalization assumed; see Section 3.)\\n- **\\\"Outperform on BBH\\\"** is operationalized as: greater aggregate BBH score under the MinED arm than under the EM arm, measured as the paired per-task mean-difference over the 27 locked tasks.\\n\\n**Operationalizing the comparison.**\\n- The two arms share exactly one backbone, one prompt string, one decoding policy, one preference dataset, one SFT checkpoint, one KL coefficient, and one optimization budget. Only the alignment criterion varies.\\n- The outcome is a 27-dimensional paired vector \\u0394_i = score^{MinED}_i \\u2212 score^{EM}_i (with optional seed-mean if multi-seed).\\n- The primary scalar is the global macro-mean over \\u0394, the global wine being the **primary pre-registered metric**.\\n- A structurally deducible **directional sanity constraint**: since EM is recoverable as MinED in the \\u03c4 \\u2192 0 limiting case (Section 4 slot v), MinED is never structurally worse than EM on a per-example basis; any aggregate gain must come from cases where EM is brittle \\u2014 primarily free-form tasks \\u2014 not from cases where EM is already saturated \\u2014 primarily MCQ tasks. This is a **structural** observation, not an empirical one, and bounds the question rather than answering it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 2 \\u2014 Experimental arms + IV/DV/covariates table\\n\\n| Element | Specification | Confirmation status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Arm A \\u2014 EM | Reward = \\ud835\\udfd9[canonical(pred) == canonical(gold)] (canonicalize per Section 3) | design default; source-paper confirmation pending |\\n| Arm B \\u2014 MinED | Reward = (1 \\u2212 normalized_edit_distance) + \\u03b5 \\u00b7 completion_bonus, gated by \\u03c4; 0 (floor) when normalized_distance > \\u03c4 | design default; source-paper confirmation pending (Section 4) |\\n| **Independent variable (IV)** | Alignment criterion \\u2208 {EM, MinED}; two-level, within-subject over tasks | locked |\\n| **Dependent variable (DV), per task** | BBH accuracy on task i \\u2208 {1,\\u2026,27} | locked |\\n| **Primary aggregate DV** | Global macro-mean over the 27 per-task accuracies | locked (pre-registered) |\\n| **Secondary aggregate DVs** | MCQ-only macro-mean (n=23); free-form-only macro-mean (n=4) | locked |\\n| Backbone (controlled, **NOT varied**) | One single fixed backbone across both arms. Designated \\\"MinED-paper-canonical, identity TBD\\\". Plausible class per documented prior: text-davinci-002 family or open-source equivalent at comparable scale. | identity pending source-paper confirmation |\\n| Demonstration protocol (PRIMARY) | BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun et al. canonical exemplars) | locked |\\n| Demonstration protocol (SECONDARY, appendix) | Zero-shot CoT (Kojima et al., \\\"Let's think step by step\\\") | locked |\\n| Decoding | Greedy | locked |\\n| Seeds | n_seeds = 1 (single-run reporting), 3 (multi-seed reporting, mean across seeds per arm per task) | locked |\\n| Prompt string | Identical byte-for-byte across both arms | locked |\\n| Pair dataset | Identical across both arms | locked |\\n| SFT starting checkpoint | Identical across both arms | locked |\\n| KL coefficient | Identical across both arms | locked |\\n| Optimization budget (steps, tokens) | Identical across both arms | locked |\\n| RLHF algorithm family (e.g., PPO, DPO, IPO) | Identical across both arms | locked |\\n\\n**Justification of foundational concept (good-faith friendliness).** A \\\"macro-mean\\\" is the unweighted mean of per-task scores; alternative is a \\\"micro-mean\\\" which weights each example equally and can be dominated by large tasks. Macro-mean is the BBH-canonical aggregate because BBH tasks have approximately equal example counts (~250 each per Suzgun-2022 documented prior), and macro-mean treats every task as an equally-weighted voice in the headline.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 3 \\u2014 BBH evaluation protocol with locked task list and MCQ/free-form split\\n\\n**Locked composition** (per study_context `iclr2024/18013/4:setup_14`):\\n- Total = 27 tasks.\\n- Subset MCQ = 23 tasks \\u2192 scored by accuracy on canonical choice letter.\\n- Subset free-form = 4 tasks \\u2192 scored by canonicalized exact-match against gold string.\\n\\n**Historical-context footnote (canonical Suzgun accounting).** Suzgun et al. 2022 (\\\"Challenging BIG-Bench Tasks and Whether Chain-of-Thought Can Solve Them\\\") names **23 task families** in prose, including reasoning (causal judgement, formal fallacies, snarks, sports understanding), algorithmic (boolean expressions, dyck languages, multistep arithmetic, navigate, word sorting, object counting), and lookup/reasoning (date understanding, hyperbaton, movie recommendation, penguins in a table, ruin names, salient translation, geometric shapes, temporal sequences, web of lies, disambiguation QA, reasoning about colored objects). The 27-task accounting used here corresponds to the BBH-YAML task-config taxonomy on the canonical BBH GitHub release, in which `logical_deduction_three_objects / five / seven` and `tracking_shuffled_objects_three_objects / five / seven` are counted as six distinct configs rather than two families. **Suzgun reference is documented prior only; not locally verifiable in this workspace.** The locked 27-task design-of-record treats canonical task names as confirmation-pending to the source-paper / experiment-script `tasks/` directory.\\n\\n**Per-task fields to populate at confirmation time** (design-stage schema, no committed values except for `default_prompt_template`):\\n\\n| Field | Default | Confirmation |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| task_id | string matching Suzgun YAML convention (e.g., `bbh:boolean_expressions`) | pending |\\n| task_name | display string | pending |\\n| task_type \\u2208 {MCQ, free-form} | as locked split | locked |\\n| n_examples | \\u2248 250 per Suzgun convention; cite exact when confirmed | pending |\\n| default_prompt_template | BBH few-shot CoT (Suzgun canonical) | locked |\\n| scoring function (MCQ) | canonical choice letter; tie-break = regex `\\\\(\\\\w\\\\)` then first uppercase token | locked as design-stage; pending comparison with Suzgun parser |\\n| scoring function (free-form) | lowercase + strip-whitespace + collapse internal ws + arithmetic numeric extraction | locked as design-stage; pending source-paper confirmation (study_context confirmation pending) |\\n\\n**Free-form scoring canonicalization (design-stage default, source-paper confirmation pending):**\\n1. Lowercase the prediction string.\\n2. Strip leading/trailing whitespace.\\n3. Collapse runs of internal whitespace to single space.\\n4. If task is arithmetic (e.g., `multistep_arithmetic_two`), extract numeric value via regex `\\u00b1?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?`; compare as floats.\\n5. Exact-string match against canonicalized gold.\\n\\n**MCQ scoring canonicalization** maps generation to (A), (B), (C), (D) \\u2026 depending on choice letter; tie-break order: regex `\\\\(\\\\w\\\\)` then first uppercase single-letter token. (Documented-prior BBH protocol; not locally verified.)\\n\\n**Held-out status (no BBH training):** BBH examples are used only for evaluation in both arms; no BBH example is consumed by SFT, RM training, or RL training. **Status**: assumed-because-prior-knowledge-of-Suzgun-BBH-design; unconfirmed-locally.\\n\\n**Decoding and seeding:** greedy, n_seeds \\u2208 {1, 3}. With n_seeds = 3, the reported per-task accuracy per arm is the mean across 3 seeds.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 4 \\u2014 MinED operationalization (default config + source-paper confirmation flags)\\n\\nThe 6 implementation slots from the reviewer's Lock 5 are tabulated with (a) locked design-stage default, (b) rationale, (c) source-paper confirmation flag.\\n\\n| Slot | Locked design-stage default | Rationale | Source-paper confirmation |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| (i) Edit-distance level | **Character-level PRIMARY** (Levenshtein over Unicode codepoints); **BPE/token-level ACCEPTABLE SECONDARY** | Char-level is tokenizer-agnostic and reproducible. BPE-level requires tokenizer alignment with backbone and so couples the metric to the backbone family. | pending |\\n| (ii) Normalization | **ratio = Levenshtein(pred, gold) / max(\\\\|gold\\\\|, \\\\|prediction\\\\|)** \\u2208 [0, 1] PRIMARY; raw Levenshtein distance as SECONDARY reporting | Bounding the metric to [0, 1] yields scale-invariant rewards interpretable as \\\"fraction of the longer string that must change to match the shorter\\\". Raw distance preserved for diagnostics. | pending |\\n| (iii) Reward formulation | `reward(pred, gold) = 1 \\u2212 normalized_distance + \\u03b5 \\u00b7 completion_bonus`, where \\u03b5 > 0 (design-stage default = 1e-3) and `completion_bonus = 1` if the generation's structural envelope matches gold (matched by length bucket: same number of structured elements as gold, e.g., equal number of closing brackets, equal number of arithmetic operands, equal number of sorted words), else 0. If `normalized_distance > \\u03c4`, the reward collapses to a floor value (default = 0). | 1 \\u2212 normalized_distance \\u2208 [0, 1] is the principal signal; \\u03b5-completion bonus prevents the policy from hacking by truncation to a sub-segment of gold; the \\u03c4-gate prevents rewarding structurally-wrong generations. | pending \\u2014 formulation matches reviewer's brief; exact \\u03b5, completion-bonus definition, and floor value to be cross-checked against source-paper |\\n| (iv) Threshold \\u03c4 | Scalar training-time gate. Design-stage \\u03c4-grid = {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0}. Each \\u03c4 is a separate sub-arm of Arm B; the headline \\u03c4 is the one maximizing primary pre-registered metric; sensitivity reported across all \\u03c4. | \\u03c4 = 0 must collapse MinED to EM (slot v); \\u03c4 = 1.0 sets the gate to \\\"always pass\\\". | pending \\u2014 paper may use a different \\u03c4 or \\u03c4-grid; cross-check required |\\n| (v) **SANITY CONTROL** = \\u03c4 \\u2192 0 \\u21d2 EM | **Pre-computation gate**: implement, run MinED with \\u03c4 = 0 on a synthetic batch (e.g., 100 hand-crafted pred/gold pairs spanning exact matches, off-by-whitespace, off-by-letter, off-by-word, fully-disjoint strings); assert reward equals EM within tolerance `\\u03b5_sanity = 1e-6` pointwise; if any assertion fails, BLOCK downstream runs and report failure. | Slot v is the only slot whose correctness can be checked without source-paper credentials \\u2014 because \\u03c4 = 0 reduces MinED to a definitional limit. Failing this gate means implementation is bugged. | confirmed-as-design-discipline |\\n| (vi) Stage of application | **Training-time reward PRIMARY**: MinED scores each minibatch's generations during RL training, providing the gradient-bearing signal. **Evaluation-time scoring SECONDARY**: under either arm's policy, evaluate using MinED-as-scorer as a diagnostic (i.e., what would MinED have said about EM-arm generations and vice versa). | Training-time is where the criterion effects policy gradients; evaluation-time secondary reporting reveals whether gains survive a metric-swap. | pending \\u2014 source-paper's split between training-time reward vs evaluation-time scorer must be confirmed |\\n\\n**Note on slot interactions.** Slots (ii) and (iii) jointly determine the reward mapping. Slot (iv) determines the active gate. The sanity control (slot v) is the only universally checkable invariant. Slots (i), (iii), (iv), (vi) together comprise what the source paper would have to document for us to use its numbers \\u2014 currently all four are confirmation-pending.\\n\\n**Cross-cutting default for the \\u03c4-floor.** When `normalized_distance > \\u03c4`, reward = 0 (the design-stage floor). Whether the source paper uses 0, a small negative, or a shaping function here is confirmation-pending.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 5 \\u2014 Statistical analysis plan with pre-registration\\n\\n### 5.1 Pre-registered primary\\n\\n- **Unit of analysis** = task (n = 27). Each task yields one paired delta \\u0394_i = score^{MinED}_i \\u2212 score^{EM}_i, aggregated across seeds as the mean (n_seeds = 3) or the single value (n_seeds = 1).\\n- **Pre-registered scalar** = global macro-mean \\u0394\\u0304 = (1/27) \\u03a3_i \\u0394_i.\\n- **Pre-registered test** = paired **Wilcoxon signed-rank**, two-sided, \\u03b1 = 0.05, on the 27 \\u0394\\u0304_i values.\\n- **Effect size** = **rank-biserial correlation r_rb** with bootstrap 95% CI computed over seeds (B = 1 000 resamples when n_seeds \\u2265 3; degenerate when n_seeds = 1 \\u2014 reported as NA).\\n- **Reportable summary** = {median \\u0394, signed-rank W, two-sided p, r_rb, 95% CI}.\\n\\n**Justification of foundational concept (good-faith friendliness).** Wilcoxon signed-rank is a non-parametric test that ranks the absolute values of pairwise differences, then sums the ranks of positive-signed differences and tests whether that sum departs significantly from its null expectation under symmetric zero-median. It is the standard paired alternative to the paired t-test when the number of pairs is small (~25), when the differences cannot be assumed Gaussian, or when the experimenter wishes to be robust to a single outlying task distorting the mean. The paired t-test, by contrast, computes (mean \\u0394) / (sd \\u0394 / \\u221an) under normality assumptions. Rank-biserial correlation r_rb = (W\\u207a \\u2212 W\\u207b)/(W\\u207a + W\\u207b), bounded in [\\u22121, +1]; a positive r_rb says more positive-signed differences, i.e., MinED > EM direction.\\n\\n### 5.2 Pre-registered secondaries\\n\\n- **MCQ-only macro-mean** \\u0394^{MCQ} over n = 23 task-deltas; same test family.\\n- **Free-form-only macro-mean** \\u0394^{FF} over n = 4 task-deltas; same test family **but UNDERPOWERED**: with n = 4 pairs, no inferential test has adequate power to reject the null under realistic effect sizes; report descriptively (point estimate, sign, range) only. Flagged explicitly as such.\\n- **Global macro-mean over per-seed triples** is identical to primary by construction; not a separate test.\\n\\n### 5.3 Exploratory status (not pre-registered; multiple-comparison caveat applies)\\n\\n- Per-task headline accuracy per arm (27 entries \\u00d7 2 arms) \\u2014 descriptive only.\\n- Per-task inference (sign test or per-task bootstrap CI) \\u2014 no family-wise correction is applied; per-task results carry an inflated false-positive warning.\\n- Stratification by sub-family (algorithmic / linguistic / logical / symbolic) \\u2014 descriptive.\\n- Stratification by demonstration pool (few-shot vs zero-shot) \\u2014 appendix only.\\n- Seed-sensitivity scatter (\\u0394\\u0304_i vs seed index) \\u2014 appendix only.\\n\\n### 5.4 Pre-registration code-level commitments\\n\\n- **Pairing rule** = per-task \\u0394_i defined once a score exists for both arms in seed s on task i; otherwise that task in seed s is dropped. Missing-task exclusion is symmetric across arms.\\n- **Cross-seed aggregation** = for n_seeds = 3, per-task \\u0394\\u0304_i is the mean across the 3 surviving per-seed \\u0394_i; a task is dropped entirely from all seeds if dropped in any seed (to preserve pairing for the final cross-seed Wilcoxon).\\n- **Determinism** = greedy decoding reduces per-seed variance to 0 for a given prompt; n_seeds > 1 in this design captures *seeds over RL training stochasticity* (e.g., minibatch shuffle seed), not decoding stochasticity.\\n\\n### 5.5 Honest small-N caveat (carried to result-stage report)\\n\\n- With N = 27 pairs, paired Wilcoxon at \\u03b1 = 0.05 two-sided achieves 80% power only at standardized effect \\u03b4/\\u03c3 \\u2248 0.55 (i.e., Cohen's d_z \\u2265 ~0.55). Smaller true effects \\u2014 even if present \\u2014 will yield non-significant p-values.\\n- N = 4 pairs (free-form subset) \\u2192 effectively zero inferential power; pre-registered as descriptive-only.\\n- Consequence: a non-significant Wilcoxon in this design does NOT establish \\\"no difference\\\", only \\\"no detectable difference at medium-to-large effect size\\\".\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 6 \\u2014 Threats to validity and mitigations\\n\\n| # | Threat | Source of threat | Mitigation locked in this design |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Backbone confound | Different backbones across arms would invalidate paired comparison | Single fixed backbone across both arms (Lock 2) |\\n| 2 | Prompt-side bias | Different prompt strings across arms | Identical byte-for-byte prompt to both arms |\\n| 3 | Demonstration exemplar bias | Different few-shot exemplars across arms | Same exemplar copy-pasted across both arms; PRIMARY = Suzgun canonical; SECONDARY = Kojima zero-shot (appendix) |\\n| 4 | Decoding stochasticity | Greedy deterministic at decoding; cross-run variance only at training-time stochasticity | Greedy default; n_seeds \\u2265 3 for cross-training-seed reporting |\\n| 5 | MCQ vs free-form scale conflation | Free-form tasks have lower absolute scores; macro-mean mixing them is a heterogeneous average | Report per-type (MCQ vs free-form) macro-mean alongside global (Section 5) |\\n| 6 | Multiple comparisons across 27 per-task tests | Inflated family-wise false-positive rate | Pre-register 1 primary (global); MCQ/FF secondaries; per-task = exploratory (Section 5.3) |\\n| 7 | Task count ambiguity (23 vs 27) | Suzgun 23-task prose vs YAML/config 27-task accounting | Anchored to 27 per study_context; Suzgun 23-task referred to in footnote only |\\n| 8 | Free-form subset underpower | n = 4 pairs | Descriptive-only on free-form sub-aggregate; primary on global 27-task |\\n| 9 | Source-paper \\u03c4-grid unverified | Source paper may report a specific \\u03c4 or \\u03c4-grid | Sensitivity report across design-stage {0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0} \\u03c4-grid (Section 4 slot iv) |\\n| 10 | Source-paper edit-distance level unverified | Char vs BPE affects reward scale and interpretation | Char primary; BPE reported as secondary (Section 4 slot i) |\\n| 11 | Source-paper reward formulation unverified | \\u03b5-completion bonus + floor penalty specifics | Design defaults committed; explicitly pending (Section 4 slot iii) |\\n| 12 | Source-paper stage of application unverified | Training-time vs evaluation-time use determines what is being compared | Design committed to training-time primary, evaluation-time secondary; both reported (Section 4 slot vi) |\\n| 13 | Sanity-control (\\u03c4=0 \\u21d2 EM) failure | Implementation bug under any of slots (i)-(iv) | Pre-execution gate blocks the run on failure (Section 4 slot v) |\\n| 14 | BBH held-out not strictly held-out | MinED paper might have trained on BBH contamination | Audit of MinED paper's training data declaration; flagged for researcher |\\n| 15 | track.md content unverified | File referenced in task.json but absent from /workspace | Quoted one-line body is the only track.md content available; treated as binding contract (\\\"design-only, no repo, no compute, no empirics\\\") |\\n| 16 | Network disabled | Cannot resurrect MinED paper / BBH script locally | Section 4's confirmation-pending column carries this liability |\\n| 17 | RLHF algorithm family not pinned | PPO vs DPO vs IPO etc. may shift baseline expectation | Identical algorithm family across arms; family identity marked \\\"locked, exact identity TBD consistent with MinED paper\\\" |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Section 7 \\u2014 Feasibility and scope-limits (derived from environment)\\n\\n### 7.1 Environment-confirmed facts (re-derived from /workspace)\\n\\n| Fact | Evidence |\\n|---|---|\\n| /workspace contains only `task.json` (390 B) | `ls -la /workspace`; sha256 = `83e037a30efe207a219988d927e3d31755f1b710202d2ae319cbeb35039459f3` |\\n| `track.md` is referenced in `task.json.documents` but is NOT on disk | `cat /workspace/track.md` \\u2192 \\\"No such file or directory\\\" |\\n| Only body of `track.md` available = its quoted one-line description | `task.json`: `documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"` |\\n| /home/actor/ exists but is empty | `ls -la /home/actor/` |\\n| No BBH JSON, no MinED paper, no harness code, no model checkpoints, no `evaluate.py`, no `tasks/` directory | `find / -maxdepth 5` filtered by bbh/mined/bigbench/hard/tasks/iclr/paper/source \\u2192 no relevant matches |\\n| Network disabled | `environment.net